<title>SINGAPORE: Exabyte expects to return to profit in Q1.</title>
<headline>Exabyte expects to return to profit in Q1.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tape storage products company Exabyte Corp said on Monday it expected to return to profit in the first quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>&quot;Yes,&quot; chairman Peter Behrendt said in response to a Reuters question on whether he expected the company to turn in a profit in the first quarter.  </p>
<p>Exabyte had reported a net loss of US$2.04 million in the last quarter of 1996.</p>
<p>Behrendt declined to make projections for the rest of 1997 but added the company expected to increase shipments of two new eight mm tape drives.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom 65-8703080</p>
